{"id": "EUVD-2026-103651", "enisaUuid": "79d72714-ca92-3ed3-ae39-d3b8152020af", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/virtio: release the GEM object on virtio_gpu_vram_create() errors\n\nvirtio_gpu_vram_create() frees the object with a bare kfree(vram) on\nboth error paths after drm_gem_private_object_init() has run, and on the\nsecond one after drm_gem_create_mmap_offset() has linked obj->vma_node\ninto the device's VMA offset manager. The freed object stays in that\ninterval tree, so a later lookup or insertion walks freed memory, and\nthe dma_resv and gpuva lock are never destroyed.\n\nCall drm_gem_object_release() before kfree() on both paths.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/977c2934064969503cabf98b1135d202ff62822e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5118b5fdf1eb9922a0cdd2afd25252081e2d4302", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9bb8f8fd5694185c2f71ff91869afb300aab392", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03bdbf182082694ab2add620d85f1a8b8f51bbbc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c2cb3dd1447752b73d4f44d6b7434bc5259bfec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c8deb77d05bcc8f79e255f669d82ec6ce91be12", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/036d28db1818af2f9d80db771f5405da84d7732d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98606", "GHSA-9vq3-mxmp-fq54"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ed6d8ba-0e41-385a-89f6-8bb446a27bc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "26757004-4ff9-3d26-a86b-dc41b96dd723", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "29bdda3c-4057-3690-9bd5-30624a545691", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11"}, {"id": "351951b5-4373-3b78-951c-1ed1e7c3a75f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_versi